Why Is Demand Increasing?
5G-Advanced infrastructure: High-speed communication equipment requires compact protection devices that preserve signal integrity while handling surge events.
EV charging growth: Electric-vehicle chargers and charging-station controllers require high-voltage protection against transient events.
Compact PCB designs: Surface-mount GDTs occupy less board space than traditional protection components.
EMC compliance: Stricter electromagnetic-compatibility standards are encouraging OEMs to adopt reliable over-voltage protection.
Industrial automation: High-density circuit designs are increasing demand for compact transient-voltage protection components.
5G, EV & Surge Protection Trends
The Surface Mount Gas Discharge Tubes Market is benefiting from the expansion of 5G-Advanced networks, EV charging infrastructure, industrial IoT, and renewable-energy power electronics. Low-capacitance SMD GDTs can provide high-energy surge protection without significantly affecting high-frequency signal performance.
High-capacity devices are gaining particular attention in outdoor telecommunications infrastructure and high-power industrial applications. At the same time, manufacturers are developing customized voltage ratings, gas formulations, and temperature ranges for emerging power-electronics applications.
